# 9. SHARED PRODUCTS AND CUSTOMERS

Products and customers belong to the business rather than individual vans.

If the owner adds a product, that product becomes available to authorized employees after synchronization.

Each van retains separate stock quantities.

Example:

Product: Milk 1 L

```text
Business Product ID: P-0001
Selling price: BHD 0.750
VAT: Configured rate

Warehouse stock: 300
Van 001 stock: 50
Van 002 stock: 70
Van 003 stock: 40
```

All salespeople view the same product definition and authorized price.

They cannot arbitrarily modify the centrally configured selling price.

A salesperson creating a new customer makes the customer available within the business according to company visibility rules.

Customer IDs must be centrally generated or safely unique.

