# 17. COMPLETE ACCEPTANCE TESTS

The multi-tenant and multi-van feature is complete only when all these scenarios pass:

1. Business A registers and activates successfully.
2. Business B registers independently.
3. Business A cannot read, update or delete Business B records.
4. Business A creates three vans.
5. Owner invites three salespeople.
6. Invitations can only be accepted by their intended verified accounts.
7. Salespeople join without entering separate company activation codes.
8. Each salesperson sees only assigned van inventory.
9. Authorized salespeople can create invoices.
10. Unauthorized supplier creation is denied at the API layer.
11. Unauthorized staff invitations are denied.
12. Owner can reassign an employee between vans.
13. The employee's effective permissions update correctly.
14. Owner can revoke an employee.
15. Revoked employee backend requests fail.
16. Two vans can sell simultaneously.
17. A same-van last-unit stock conflict cannot oversell.
18. Repeated checkout requests do not create duplicate invoices.
19. Offline queued operations survive application restart.
20. Reconnected devices reconcile their queued operations correctly.
21. Company-wide sales totals reconcile to committed invoices.
22. Inventory totals reconcile to the movement ledger.
23. Business switching never exposes another company's cached records.
24. Employees cannot escalate their own roles or permissions.
25. Real Android devices complete sign-in, invitation, van assignment and sales workflows successfully.

These must be tested against the actual deployed authorization and transactional backend, not only using local mocks.

